.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DSA_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DSA_new ,
.Nm DSA_free
.Nd allocate and free DSA objects
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/dsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft DSA*
.Fo DSA_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo DSA_free
.Fa "DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_free 3 .
.Pp
.Fn DSA_new
allocates and initializes a
.Vt DSA
structure.
It is equivalent to calling DSA_new_method(NULL).
.Pp
.Fn DSA_free
frees the
.Vt DSA
structure and its components.
The values are erased before the memory is returned to the system.
If
.Fa dsa
is NULL nothing is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If the allocation fails,
.Fn DSA_new
returns
.Dv NULL
and sets an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
Otherwise it returns a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_free
returns no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_free 3 ,
.Xr DSA_new 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr DSA_generate_parameters 3 ,
.Xr DSA_generate_key 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
